# deny.txt — the private wordlist check-public.sh refuses to run without.
#
# COPY THIS TO ~/.config/kontor/deny.txt AND FILL IT IN. Never commit the
# filled-in version, to this repository or any other: a public file listing
# the names you are protecting publishes the names.
#
# One term per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Matching is whole-word and case-insensitive, so ordinary words are safe to
# list. A branch named after an ordinary noun will not match that noun with a
# suffix attached, but it WILL match every innocent use of the bare word.
# That false positive is the price of catching the real one, and it is worth
# paying: this repository has twice reworded innocent prose rather than
# weaken the list.
#
# Branch names do NOT belong here. check-public.sh reads those straight from
# branches.conf, including hyphen/underscore variants, so that a branch can
# never be missed because nobody remembered to type it. This file is for
# everything the config does not already know:
#
#   - people: correspondents, colleagues, family, opposing parties
#   - organisations: employers, clients, schools, authorities, insurers
#   - matters: the short name you use for an ongoing case or process
#   - places specific enough to identify a person
#
# If the gate blocks on a term here and the text is genuinely innocent,
# reword the text. Do not remove the term. That trade has been made twice in
# this repository's history and the reword was the right call both times.
